{"id":"s3.1.9","slug":"square-root-approximations","title":"Finding Approximations of Square Roots","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Approximating square and cube roots of large numbers is a common task. One method is to factor out powers of 100 (for square roots) or 1000 (for cube roots) from under the radical to simplify the problem.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For example, $\\sqrt{1234567} \\approx \\sqrt{1230000} = \\sqrt{123 \\times 100 \\times 100} = 100\\sqrt{123} \\approx 100 \\times 11 = 1100$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For finding exact cube roots, like $\\sqrt[3]{830584}$:</p><ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 mb-4\"><li>Group digits in threes from the right (830, 584). This indicates a two-digit answer.</li><li>The last digit of the number is 4. Since $4^3 = 64$, the units digit of the root is 4.</li><li>The first group is 830. Since $9^3 = 729 < 830$ and $10^3 = 1000 > 830$, the tens digit is 9.</li></ol><p>The answer is 94.</p>","summary":"Approximating square and cube roots of large numbers is a common task.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem asking for the approximation of a square or cube root of a large number.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Approximate $\\sqrt{15376}$.","answer":"124","kind":"approximate","tags":["algebra","logs-exponents"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $\\sqrt[3]{830584}$.","answer":"94","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra","logs-exponents"]},{"id":3,"text":"Approximate $\\sqrt{23456}$.","answer":"153","kind":"approximate","tags":["algebra","logs-exponents"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":4,"text":"Approximate $\\sqrt{32905}$.","answer":"181","kind":"approximate","tags":["algebra","logs-exponents"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":5,"text":"Approximate $\\sqrt{6543210}$.","answer":"2558","kind":"approximate","tags":["algebra","logs-exponents"],"hasErrorRange":true},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $\\sqrt[3]{658503}$.","answer":"87","kind":"exact","tags":["algebra","logs-exponents"]},{"id":7,"text":"Approximate $\\sqrt{6213457}$.","a